 Mission 
 The Environmental Stewardship Committee’s mission is to promote environmental health and sustainability through awareness, education, and initiatives that will empower community members to be change agents for a greener, more environmentally friendly Easton.  
 Goals 

 Work with the Town of Easton departments and committees to support environmental goals and amplify the Town’s messaging to the public. 
 Foster opportunities and partnerships with community members, businesses, and other approved entities that result in synergistic efforts to protect natural resources and the health and quality of life in Easton, MA. 
 Support programs that help the town in various ways: 




 Conserve and protect our water sources 
 Reduce and manage waste in ways that are positive to the environment 
 Promote alternative energy use to align with Massachusetts’ Clean Energy and Climate Plan goals 
 Minimize and reduce the use of harmful and dangerous pesticides or practices that hurt vital ecosystems 
 Participate in discussions about climate change and how to address in town 
 Educate the public about environmental issues and sustainability practices 




 Meet monthly to discuss outreach, initiatives, and news that affect the Town of Easton. Present important findings to key officials. 
 Explore all ways to get messages to the public through social media, local cable television, the town website, town newsletter, printed flyers, and an online directory of services. Also, appear at appropriate public-facing events or meetings when possible. 

 View the charge for the Environmental Stewardship Committee. 
 Information and Links 
 Resources for a More Sustainable Easton: Live More Sustainably to Conserve Resources and Protect Easton’s Natural Beauty This guide was created to share resources with Easton residents and businesses to help identify ways to save energy, protect water and land, and reduce the amount of waste produced.  
 View the 2026 revised guide with resources for a more sustainable Easton. Easton’s Green Communities Committee information can be found here.  REDUCE/REUSE/RECYCLE At the Special Town Meeting on November 12, 2019, Easton approved Article 9 to ban the distribution of plastic shopping bags at checkout counters in town.  Here is a link to Article 9  which is currently in effect. Please bring your own reusable bags to shop and to help reduce waste and recycling contamination in our town.  Questions about recycling? Check out the  Recyclopedia at Recycle Smart MA . 
