 Easton’s  Hazardous Household Waste Collection Day  usually happens in the Spring. Interested in composting?  You may be able to get a low-cost compost bin  from one of our neighboring towns. See  this flyer  for more information on setting up your own home composting bins. CLEANER WATER INITIATIVES What are PFAS and how can we reduce our exposure to this family of chemicals?   The Path Forward on PFAS: Examining State and Local Approaches - Easton  was presented to the Green Communities Committee on January 17, 2023 by Connor Read, Easton Town Administrator and MMA Designee to The Massachusetts PFAS Interagency Taskforce. It provides an excellent overview of the scale of the problem and some steps the town and state are taking to address this issue. In addition, visit the town's dedicated  PFAS information page  for additional developments and information. Before watering your lawn, get information on town water restrictions at  Easton’s Water Restrictions Page . Easton’s Conservation Commission has published  Sustainable Lawn Care Guidelines  to help residents maintain their lawns with less negative impact on the environment. Make your lawn more tolerant to drought or lawn watering restrictions by downloading this  list of drought-tolerant plants that are native to Massachusetts . ENERGY SAVINGS Schedule your no-cost MassSave  Home Energy Assessment  for residents, landlords, and businesses. Qualified low-income families should contact  Self Help Inc  for financial assistance on a number of energy-saving programs. Use 100% National Wind Renewable Energy Certificates to power your home: Learn more about  Easton’s Optional Green Product  within the town’s Community Choice Power Supply Program. The latest information  on the Solar Massachusetts Renewable Target (SMART) Program can be found  here .  And get competitive quotes on solar power for your home or business using  EnergySage  to research and shop for solar. Get a better idea of how much electricity your home is using with the Ames Free Library's  Home Energy Meter Loan Program . Borrow a Kill-A-Watt EZ Electricity Usage Monitor from the  Library of Things . Visit  this guide  to energy rebates and incentives available in Massachusetts.  
